  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 156 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nCurrent surface analysis places deepening low over Colorado into\nWyoming, while tilted ridge remains orientated through the Great\nLakes into Ontario/central Manitoba. Upper level analysis places\ndeep trough approaching the western fringes of the Rockies, with\na low remaining closed off over Nevada. Over our area, moist \nsouth/southeast flow continues to keep low cloud cover \nthroughout the state while temperatures remain quite mild. \n\nFor tonight, surface low will continue to deepen before ejecting\nout over Nebraska overnight, nudging into central South Dakota,\nas upper trough slides over the Rockies. Precipitation that is\nalready starting to develop over western South Dakota nudging\ninto southeast Montana will continue to push northeasterly and\nspread out in coverage. As we go through the night, rain showers\nwill eventually push throughout the state.\n\nOn Monday, low gradually lifts to the southeast crossing near\nthe intersection of ND/SD/MN late afternoon into the early\nevening, while upper trough pushes easterly and starts to close\noff nearly stacking the system. Widespread rain continues\nthrough the day before starting to taper off over the west\novernight as the low slides into Minnesota. Low then loiters\nover Minnesota for Tuesday. The overall track of the system is \na bit slower and stretching a bit further west. Therefore, \nrainfall chances have broadened and increased. Latest NBM \nguidance is now giving about an 80 percent or greater chance of \nseeing one inch or more of rain along and south of Interstate \n94, and a 60 percent or greater chance of seeing two inches or \nmore along and southeast of a line from Jamestown to Wishek. \n\nAlong with the precipitation, winds will be on the increase\nlater Monday into Monday night as the low lifts on its way.\nLatest NBM continues to suggest the possibility of advisory\ncriteria wind gusts (45 mph) over mainly the southern 1/3 of our\narea, but a look at forecast soundings continues to show\nquestion as to whether this could be realized given lack of\nmixing. Therefore, will hold off on any products for now and\ngive it another look overnight.  \n\nQuieter weather sets up over the area mid-week, though a few\nrain showers remain possible on Wednesday over our eastern\nlocations given the loitering low over Minnesota. Mainly dry\nconditions then expected through he remainder of the week, with\nnear to above average temperatures.",
